From: 77450danik <dnsystems@email.ua>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dwrite: Latin, Cyrillic and Greek fall back to Segoe UI, as in Windows.

The system fallback gave Tahoma for Latin and Cyrillic, and nothing for
Greek: text a page's fonts lack (Cyrillic in a font of Latin only) came
out in Wine's Tahoma, which Chrome drew as Windows XP did. Windows falls
back to Segoe UI; Arctic makes that a family of its UI font (Personalization
writes Fonts\Replacements), Tahoma stays after it.
---
diff --git a/dlls/dwrite/analyzer.c b/dlls/dwrite/analyzer.c
--- a/dlls/dwrite/analyzer.c
+++ b/dlls/dwrite/analyzer.c
@@ -232,12 +232,16 @@
 }
 system_fallback_config[] =
 {
-    /* Latin, Combining Diacritical Marks */
+    /* Latin, Combining Diacritical Marks: Segoe UI, as in Windows (Arctic
+       makes it a family of its UI font, Fonts\Replacements) */
     { "0000-007F, 0080-00FF, 0100-017F, 0180-024F, "
-      "0250-02AF, 02B0-02FF, 0300-036F", L"Tahoma" },
+      "0250-02AF, 02B0-02FF, 0300-036F", L"Segoe UI, Tahoma" },
+
+    /* Greek and Coptic, Greek Extended */
+    { "0370-03FF, 1F00-1FFF",   L"Segoe UI, Tahoma" },
 
     /* Cyrillic, Cyrillic Supplement */
-    { "0400-052F",              L"Tahoma" },
+    { "0400-052F",              L"Segoe UI, Tahoma" },
 
     { "0530-058F, FB10-FB1C",   L"Noto Sans Armenian" },
 
